+
+# Make applyPatch conform to RFC 6902
+
+## Request
+
+Users of `applyPatch` report surprising results: some patches they consider invalid are accepted, some
+edge cases give results they did not expect, and a patch that fails does not always behave the way the
+standard reads. Review how patches are checked and applied, and make the behaviour conform to RFC 6902 in
+every case, errors included.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- A patch that is not a JSON Patch throws, including an element of the patch that is a hole of a sparse
+  array.
+- The `value` of `add`, `replace` and `test` must be a JSON value; `undefined`, `NaN`, an infinity and
+  other non-JSON values throw.
+- `replace` sets an object member in place, so that the member keeps its position, as `add` does.
+- The existing tests of `applyPatch` still pass, and each defect above has a test.
